{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.ComplexDilogarithmLanden","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.ComplexDilogarithmLanden","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.ComplexDilogarithmDeriv"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.landenCombo_ofReal_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.landenCombo_ofReal_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":224,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmLanden.lean#L224-L256","doc":"**Landen's identity on the negative reals**, constant and all:\n\n    Li₂(t) + Li₂(t/(t−1)) + ½·log(1−t)² = 0   for every real `t < 0`.\n\nThe derivative is zero by `hasDerivAt_landenCombo`; the constant is `0` because\nthe combination vanishes at `0` and `Ico t 0` excludes the one point where the\nderivative hypotheses fail. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.continuousOn_landenCombo_ofReal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.continuousOn_landenCombo_ofReal","kind":"theorem","line":185,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmLanden.lean#L185-L222","doc":"**`landenCombo` is continuous along the closed negative axis, up to and\nincluding `0`.** The endpoint is the point of the lemma: the derivative fails\nthere (`z ≠ 0` is one of `hasDerivAt_landenCombo`'s hypotheses), but continuity\ndoes not, and continuity is all the constancy theorem needs at the endpoint.\n\n⚠ No hypothesis on `t`. A first version carried `ht : t ≤ 0` and Lean flagged it\nunused — correctly: continuity is checked pointwise on `Icc t 0`, and each point\nof that set already satisfies `s ≤ 0` from its own membership. For `t > 0` the\nset is empty and the statement is vacuously true, so dropping the bound\ngeneralises rather than weakens. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.one_sub_ofReal_mem_slitPlane","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.one_sub_ofReal_mem_slitPlane","kind":"theorem","line":178,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmLanden.lean#L178-L183","doc":"`1 − s` is on the slit plane for real `s ≤ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.ofReal_mem_notCut_of_nonpos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.ofReal_mem_notCut_of_nonpos","kind":"theorem","line":174,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmLanden.lean#L174-L176","doc":"`(s : ℂ) ∈ notCut` for real `s ≤ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.landenArg_mem_notCut","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.landenArg_mem_notCut","kind":"theorem","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmLanden.lean#L164-L172","doc":"`s/(s-1) ∈ notCut` for real `s ≤ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.ofReal_sub_one_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.ofReal_sub_one_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmLanden.lean#L156-L162","doc":"`(s : ℂ) − 1 ≠ 0` for real `s ≤ 0` — used on every branch below. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.landenArg_lt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.landenArg_lt_one","kind":"theorem","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmLanden.lean#L149-L154","doc":"For real `s ≤ 0` the Landen substitution lands in `[0,1)` — in particular\noff `Li₂`'s cut. This is the one inequality the whole argument turns on. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.landenCombo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.landenCombo","kind":"def","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmLanden.lean#L145-L147","doc":"The Landen combination. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.hasDerivAt_landenCombo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.hasDerivAt_landenCombo","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmLanden.lean#L93-L128","doc":"**The Landen combination is locally constant.**\n\n`d/dz [Li₂(z) + Li₂(z/(z−1)) + ½·log(1−z)²] = 0`. The `slitPlane` hypothesis is\nwhere the branch is pinned: without it `log(1 − z/(z−1))` need not be\n`−log(1−z)`, and the cancellation fails. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.arg_ne_pi_of_slitPlane","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.arg_ne_pi_of_slitPlane","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmLanden.lean#L84-L91","doc":"`arg (1−z) ≠ π` on the slit plane — the branch condition, isolated. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.hasDerivAt_landenArg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.hasDerivAt_landenArg","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmLanden.lean#L75-L82","doc":"The derivative of the Landen substitution. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.one_sub_landen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.one_sub_landen","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmLanden.lean#L68-L73","doc":"`1 − z/(z−1) = 1/(1−z)` — the substitution Landen turns on. ","signatureChunk":0}]}